+## Cloud Saves wire context
+
+Every `save`, `delete`, `prepare`, `commit`, `abort` and `restore` request carries
+an observed generation string. A JSON save body is:
+
+```json
+{"action":"save","generation":"<observed generation>","expectedRevision":0,"operationId":"<UUID>","schemaVersion":1,"metadata":{},"data":{"level":1}}
+```
+
+Persist the payload, generation, revision and operation ID together, scoped to the
+original player. Exact replay is guaranteed for the latest 3,072 completed
+operations that are also less than 30 days old. Stale context requires explicit
+reconciliation with a new operation; never silently refresh an old intent.
+Save errors additionally include `SAVE_CONFLICT` (409, with current state and
+generation), `SAVE_NOT_FOUND` (404), `INVALID_SAVE` (400),
+`SAVE_QUOTA_EXCEEDED` (413) and `STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE` (503).
+Save bodies allow 2 MiB transport overhead; JSON data is at most 1 MiB and may have
+a lower configured quota. Binary bytes use private Storage after preparation.
+See [Cloud Saves](Cloud-Saves) for action shapes, uploads and offline handling.
