@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# Supagame AI agent skill
+
+The official `supagame` skill helps coding agents integrate Supagame into your own
+game: setup, leaderboards, score-based achievements, live leaderboards, Cloud Saves,
+diagnostics and upgrades. It covers the TypeScript SDK and the HTTP/OpenAPI path
+for Unity, Godot, Unreal and custom clients. It does not invent native SDKs or
+replace your engine's project conventions.
+
+## Install in your game repository
+
+Get a trusted Supagame source checkout matching your installation. Copy the
+**whole directory**, including its `references/` files (POSIX shell example):
+
+```sh
+mkdir -p /path/to/your-game/.agents/skills
+cp -R /path/to/supagame/.agents/skills/supagame /path/to/your-game/.agents/skills/
+```
+
+Check for an existing destination first; review differences before updating a
+customized copy. The authoritative source is
+[`.agents/skills/supagame/` in the Supagame repository](https://github.com/RetroBreeze/supagame/tree/main/.agents/skills/supagame).
+It is a portable [Agent Skills](https://agentskills.io/specification) directory.
+
+[Codex discovers repository skills in `.agents/skills`](https://developers.openai.com/codex/skills).
+Other compatible coding agents can install the same folder using their supported
+skill path or installer. Follow that agent's reload instructions and check that
+`supagame` appears in its available skills. Keeping the skill only in the Supagame
+source checkout does not make it available in a different game repository.
+The npm packages do not install or activate the skill.
+
+## Invoke
+
+In Codex, use `$supagame`; in another compatible agent, use its skill selector or
+ask explicitly to use the Supagame skill. For example:
+
+- “Use $supagame to add a leaderboard to this browser game.”
+- “Use the supagame skill to integrate Cloud Saves into my Godot project.”
+- “Use $supagame to check this deployment and plan an upgrade.”
+
+The agent should inspect your existing project/Auth/configuration, explain the
+smallest change, and verify the result. Cloud Saves guidance includes generation
+context, finite retry guarantees and explicit offline conflict decisions.
+For hosted deployment it must show the exact destination and actual dry-run
+preview and obtain your authorization. A request to integrate a feature is not
+permission to deploy it.
+
+The [validation record](https://github.com/RetroBreeze/supagame/blob/main/docs/verification/AGENT-SKILL.md)
+distinguishes exercised CLI/SDK/Godot checks from scenario walkthroughs and untested
+platforms. Keep copied skills aligned with backend and SDK upgrades.
