+## Cloud Saves after an upgrade
+
+`INVALID_SAVE` from an old raw writer can mean missing `generation`. Durable SDK
+writes supplying `operationId` must also supply their originally observed generation.
+Do not fill old queued operations with today's generation to get them accepted.
+
+For `SAVE_CONFLICT`, preserve the payload/Blob and original options, review current
+cloud state, and explicitly create a new intent with its paired generation/revision.
+Offline `resolve`, `resolveBinary` and `resolveDelete` preserve replaced queues in
+local history; `sync` sends the newly chosen intent afterward. Exact replay covers
+the latest 3,072 completed operations that are also younger than 30 days; a lost
+response is not proof of failure. See [Cloud Saves](Cloud-Saves) and
+[Account recovery](Account-Recovery) for migration and conflict handling.
+
